---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Driveway Mechanic handles browser preferences, hosting, and links to other websites."
  noIndex={true}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-foreground mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/60 mb-8">
        <strong>Last updated:</strong> October 22, 2026
      </p>

      <p>
        The Driveway Mechanic provides articles without visitor accounts, a contact form, comments, or a newsletter signup.
      </p>

      <h2>Browser preference</h2>
      <p>
        The light and dark theme control saves your choice in your browser so it can restore that display preference on your next visit. You can change it with the theme control or clear the saved preference through your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics, advertising, and hosting</h2>
      <p>
        We have not added analytics tags or advertising scripts to the site's pages.
        Vercel hosts this site. Its infrastructure processes website requests, which can include your IP address and information about your device or browser.
        Vercel describes its handling of website traffic information in its <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice" class="text-accent hover:underline">Privacy Notice</a>.
        We have not yet verified the retention periods or optional data settings for this site's hosting account.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>
        Articles may link to manufacturers, retailers, or other websites. If you follow a link, the destination's privacy practices apply to your visit there. We do not control those sites. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure" class="text-accent hover:underline">affiliate disclosure</a> for how we describe paid product relationships.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
